Cut 2 design, addendum: a code audit of the lander, done because the Orchestrator asked for it.
A read-only pass over merge.py, ci_landing.py, landing_gate.py, landing_guard.py, landing_lock.py, worktree*.py, remote_branches.py and the cmd_worktree handlers listed 75 side effects and checks.
Mapping of the 75 rows: keep 23, workspace worktree adapter 22, delivery direct adapter 9, delivery pr adapter 3, delivery queue adapter 1, landing-verification writer 3, drop 15. One row counts twice.
Dropped, because GitHub's PR and required checks replace them: landing.lock and unlock and the lock across the whole queue, the merge-tree probe, the landing subject capture, workflow discovery and dispatch, ci-proofs.json, run polling, the input re-check before the merge, and the -D squash comparison.
Moved to the direct adapter: the local merge under the reference-transaction guard, its receipts, the attribution trailers and the base push.
Kept in core: the record binding, the bead checks, frozen tracker paths, the engine-stable guard, local verify and its triage, the local_only checks, the orch notes, the timings and gate_override.
The audit found 9 jobs that are not among the 4:
- the human gate override and rework loop;
- landing order by dependencies and coupling notes;
- scope policing of the paths a lane touches;
- branch freshness repair, which refreshes the generated files;
- the self-hosting engine guard;
- telemetry and orch notes;
- the release-note debt gate;
- the input fingerprint;
- dependency provisioning for each checkout.
Each of the 9 stays in core or in its adapter. Freshness repair becomes a step of the pr adapter ("update branch" plus regenerate), because GitHub has nothing for generated files.
Council pending, gate removals that are not built until a council decides each one:
- (G1) dropping the local full verify before a landing;
- (G2) dropping the lane size ceiling;
- (G3) dropping the CI rerun cap and the first-attempt-pass rule (rows 38 and 42).
Correction to section 2: GitHub's merge queue is not available for basicly. Its owner is a user account (gh api owner.type User). The docs name organization repositories only (managing-a-merge-queue, checked 2026-11-26). basicly uses pr with "Require branches to be up to date"; queue stays an adapter for organization repositories.
Step 1, now filed and built: the pr delivery adapter beside the lander. It removes nothing.
